{
  "name": "Process orders idempotently with a data table and a sub-workflow",
  "nodes": [
    {
      "parameters": {
        "content": "## Process orders idempotently with a data table and a sub-workflow\n\n### How it works\n\nThis sub-workflow receives an order from a parent workflow and uses a data table to determine whether the order ID has already been processed. If the order is new, it records a pending state, calls an external processing API, marks the order as completed, and returns the processed result. If the order was already handled, it skips processing and returns a skipped-style result through the shared final output path.\n\n### Setup steps\n\n- Configure the parent workflow to call this sub-workflow with the expected order fields, especially a unique order_id.\n- Create or select the n8n data table used to store order IDs and processing status, with columns for pending/completed state and timestamps as needed.\n- Configure the HTTP Request node with the correct processing API URL, authentication credentials, headers, and request body mapping.\n- Verify the Set nodes return the fields expected by the parent workflow.\n\n### Customization\n\nYou can adapt the idempotency key, stored status values, API endpoint, and returned fields to match your order system.",
        "width": 480,
        "height": 784
      },
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.stickyNote",
      "typeVersion": 1,
      "position": [
        -608,
        -160
      ],
      "id": "5e49efd8-1b5c-4f71-9129-35eb7285941e",
      "name": "Sticky Note"
    },
    {
      "parameters": {
        "content": "## Receive and lookup order\n\nAccepts the order from the parent workflow and checks the data table for an existing record with the same order ID.",
